      "id": 1,
      "text": "Weymouth, Massachusetts, traces its roots back to 1622 when settlers founded the Wessagusset colony, making it the state's second-oldest township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.weymouth.ma.us/2193/History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from Weymouth, Dorset in England, echoing its settlers’ homeland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weymouth%2C_Massachusetts"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The discovery of bog iron in 1837 sparked the founding of the Weymouth Iron Works Company, a key industrial milestone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
